/E (With so many servos and moving parts in this subsystem, wiring was a major challenge. Though the design of the arm itself only went through 1 iteration, our cable management has drastically improved. Now every cable is shielded, and we use hard plastic to support the cable where it connects to the servo.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
755 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 383 0 R
/T (Base Joint)
/E (Base Joint)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
756 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 383 0 R
/E (The base joint is powered by 2 Axon MAX servos that are mounted to the linear using 2 aluminum plates. These plates also attach to the extension linkage)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
757 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 383 0 R
/T ( Wrist Joint)
/E ( Wrist Joint)
/Pg 19 0 R
